<rml>
<head>
    <title>Word search HUD</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="hud.rcss" />
</head>
<body id="word-hud">
    <!-- Source: projects/word/src/gameplay/WordSearch.cpp, WordSearch::Draw.
         These containers are intentionally empty: word_data_1.wrd is not
         present in this checkout. Populate them from the actual WordBox and
         Words_Found snapshot rather than displaying invented puzzle data.

         For each Words_Found[i], append a div.word-entry to found-words.
         Set its text to the word, or to ->WORD<- when i == Selected_Word.
         Use text nodes (or escape markup) for the literal arrow characters.
         List entries advance 13px vertically; do not add buttons or headings.

         For each visible solution letter at column x and row y, append a
         div.solution-cell to solution-cells with left:26*x px; top:26*y px.
         Source coordinates follow the word's start and locale->Dir values.

         For each WordBox letter at column x and row y, append a
         div.letter-cell to puzzle-letters with left:26*x px; top:26*y px.
         Its only text is WordBox::Get_Letter(x,y).

         Keep existing arrow-key selection, Space solution toggling, and
         Escape shutdown in game input. This document has no click events.
         hud.rcss loads college-hud from assets/fonts/DejaVuSans.ttf.
         Launch with the repository root as the working directory.
    -->
    <div id="found-words"></div>
    <div id="solution-cells"></div>
    <div id="puzzle-letters"></div>
</body>
</rml>
